Subject: [sshmap fork 0003] alternate screen buffer (private modes 47/1047/1048/1049)

Provenance: semantics of upstream pyte PR #212 "Alternate screen buffer", author
            dwgx, closed WITHOUT merge on 2026-08-14 (issue #90, open since 2017).
            Differentially verified against tmux 3.6b and GNU screen (see
            PYTE82_AUDIT.md patch B). pyte is LGPL-3.0 — attribution to the PR
            author (dwgx) in this header and in code comments is MANDATORY.
Implemented: v1.2.12 as SshmapHistoryScreen overrides (sshmap); moved verbatim into
            the forked screens.py in v1.3rc1: ALTSCREEN_MODES (class attribute of
            Screen — subclasses see it via MRO); Screen.set_mode/reset_mode hooks
            -> _enter_alt/_exit_alt; state fields in Screen.__init__ (BEFORE
            self.reset()); HistoryScreen.reset — RIS inside alt = full reset + exit;
            HistoryScreen.index/reverse_index — lines scrolled off the alt buffer do
            not enter scrollback (like less). One in_alt flag (47l exits a screen
            entered via 1049h); entry idempotent; cursor NOT homed on entry; cursor
            saved/restored only for 1048/1049 (xterm: 1049 = 1047+1048) in a separate
            _alt_cursor field, NOT the savepoints stack; exit clips the saved buffer
            to current width (resize safety); alt contents do not survive the
            round-trip.
Base:       pyte 0.8.2, pyte/screens.py.
Policy:     PERMANENT — PR #212 was never merged; upstream will not absorb this patch.
Applied:    2026-09-10, sshmap v1.3rc1.

